1b:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-xs space-y-8 transition-colors duration-200","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 tracking-tight","children":["Comprehensive Islamic Waqt & Mosque Guidelines in ","Dhaka"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed","children":["Offering daily Salah on time is an essential religious obligation. For residents and visitors across ","Dhaka",", understanding how the five daily prayer intervals are calibrated to local geography ensures worship is performed with peace of heart and strict adherence to the Prophetic Sunnah."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed","children":["Situated at coordinates ",23.8103,"° N latitude and ",90.4125,"° E longitude, ","Dhaka"," experiences unique solar trajectories throughout the annual solar calendar. In this dedicated municipal briefing, we analyze the local waqt boundaries, congregational Jamat practices, and seasonal prayer transitions."]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100","children":["1. Understanding the Five Daily Waqt Boundaries in ","Dhaka"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700/60","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 block text-sm mb-1","children":["Fajr Waqt & Sehri Cutoff (","4:44 AM"," to ","6:00 AM",")"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":["Fajr commences when the true astronomical dawn (*Subh Sadiq*) appears as a horizontal white band of light stretching across the eastern horizon. For fasting during Ramadan or voluntary fasts, all food, beverage, and smoking must terminate prior to the entry of Fajr. Fajr waqt expires promptly when the upper edge of the sun crosses the horizon (Sunrise at ","6:00 AM",")."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700/60","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 block text-sm mb-1","children":["Dhuhr Waqt (","11:45 AM",")"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":["Dhuhr begins when the sun passes the meridian (*Zawal*). To avoid praying during the prohibited zenith instant, our timetable incorporates a standard 2-minute safety precaution. In local masajid across ","Dhaka",", congregational Dhuhr is commonly held between 1:15 PM and 1:30 PM."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700/60","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 block text-sm mb-1","children":["Asr Waqt (","3:49 PM",")"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed","children":"Asr commences according to the juristic school of choice. Under the Shafi’i, Maliki, and Hanbali standard, Asr starts when an object’s shadow equals its length plus noon shadow. Under the Hanafi standard followed across South Asia, Asr begins when the shadow reaches twice the object’s length plus noon shadow."}]]}],"$L23","$L24"]}]]}],"$L25","$L26"]}]
1c:["$","$L27",null,{"items":[{"question":"What time is today Fajr in Dhaka?","answer":"Today Fajr prayer in Dhaka starts at 4:44 AM (the onset of Subh Sadiq at an 18° solar depression angle) and concludes at Sunrise (6:00 AM). Fasting individuals must cease eating and drinking prior to 4:44 AM."},{"question":"What time is today Maghrib (Iftar) in Dhaka?","answer":"Today Maghrib prayer and Iftar time in Dhaka is at 5:25 PM at the precise instant the upper limb of the solar disk sets below the western horizon."},{"question":"Which calculation method is followed in Dhaka?","answer":"Prayer times in Dhaka are calculated using the KARACHI standard with an 18°/18° twilight angle and local latitude/longitude coordinates (23.8103° N, 90.4125° E)."},{"question":"What is the difference between Hanafi and Shafi'i Asr time in Dhaka?","answer":"In Dhaka, Hanafi Asr time begins approximately 45 to 60 minutes after Shafi'i Asr time due to the 2x versus 1x shadow factor calculation. Use our widget toggle above to view both schedules."},{"question":"What is the tahajjud namaz time dhaka today?","answer":"Tahajjud namaz time dhaka begins after the completion of Isha prayer and extends until the onset of Subh Sadiq (Fajr Sehri cutoff at 4:44 AM). The most virtuous period is the final third of the night, which in Dhaka typically commences between 2:45 AM and 3:30 AM depending on seasonal night length."},{"question":"What are the prohibited prayer times in Dhaka?","answer":"Prayer (including voluntary Nafl) is strictly prohibited during three periods: 1) Sunrise until 15-20 minutes thereafter; 2) Exactly at solar zenith (Zawal) for 5 minutes prior to Dhuhr; 3) The 15 minutes before Maghrib sunset when the sun turns pale yellow."},{"question":"How does daylight duration vary throughout the year in Dhaka?","answer":"Located at latitude 23.8103° N, Dhaka experiences seasonal daylight shifts between the June summer solstice and the December winter solstice. Fasting durations and waqt intervals adjust progressively through each astronomical season."}],"title":"Frequently Asked Questions for Dhaka Namaz Timings"}]
